===============================
BUILD AND INSTALL EZAPP ON ANDROID
===============================

Steps:
- ./setup
- make build_debug
- make install_debug   (first connect adb)

The ./setup script does the following:
- downloads SDL3 and SDL3_ttf source code
- extract SDL3 source code
- creates template SDL3 build directory, using script 
    /build-scripts/create-android-project.py 
- extracts SDL3_ttf source to
    SDL3-3.2.28/build/org.sthaid.ezApp/app/jni/SDL3_ttf-3.2.2/
- downloads external SDL3_ttf packages by using the download.sh script 
    SDL3-3.2.28/build/org.sthaid.ezApp/app/jni/SDL3_ttf-3.2.2/external/download.sh
- update/add files; 
  . the files in SDL3-3.2.28/build/org.sthaid.ezApp/app are replaced with 
    symlinks to the files in setup_files
  . the original files are saved to setup_files/orig
  . the setup_files/diff_against_orig script is available to view the changes,
    using meld
- ezApp source code files are symlinked to app/jni/src
- ezApp assets directory symlink is created in app/src/main

===============================
ADB SETUP
===============================

Install adb
- sudo apt install adb

Enable developer mode by tapping build number 8 times.
  Settings -> About Phone -> Software Information -> Build Number

Go to Developer Options , and enable
- Stay Awake
- USB Debugging

Connect USB data cable. And select 'allow access' on the device.
- verify connection: 'adb shell'

To use adb over Wifi, without USB cable ...

With USB cable plugged in, run cmd 
- adb tcpip 5555
- should see message "restarting in TCP mode port: 5555"

Disconnect USB cable.

Issue the adb connect cmd:
- adb connect 192.168.1.243:5555
- verify using 'adb shell'

Suggestions:
- plug phone in with power cable, to disable sleeping while charging.
- configure router to assign a static IP address to your Android device
- configure your Android device so it doesn't change its MAC address,
  when using a trusted router:
    Connections -> Wifi -> Gear -> View More -> MAC Address Type -> Pnone MAC

===============================
ADB COMMAND EXAMPLES
===============================

adb help

adb logcat --help
adb logcat -c -b all                      # clear Android log
adb logcat -s SDL SDL/APP AndroidRuntime  # view logs from SDL SDL/APP AndroidRuntime components

adb shell  # run remote shell
adb shell getprop ro.product.cpu.abi  # get Application Binary Interface

adb kill-server    # kill and start adb server
adb start-server

adb tcpip 5555    # restart Android Debug Bridge Daemon listening on TCP port 5555
adb connect 192.168.1.205:5555  # connect to device
adb devices       # list connected devices

